{{Weapons of mass destruction}}'''[[Balisca]]''' is one of a handful of countries that have historically pursued nuclear weaponry, and currently {{W|Nuclear latency|maintains the capability to produce nuclear weaponry}}. The country is a signatory of the [[w:Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty|Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty]], which it acceded to in 1992. In 2020, Balisca ratified the {{W|Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons}}, becoming the first country to have had nuclear weapons, destroyed them, and gone on to sign the treaty.  

Balisca had been aware of several country's intentions to develop nuclear capabilities since the 1950s, and actively worked to derail the efforts of those in the [[Western Hemisphere]] to gain [[W:Gas centrifuge|centrifuge technology]] that could be used to produce [[W:Enriched uranium|high-enriched uranium]] for nuclear weapons. The [[Baliscan nuclear program]] was born out of fears of quickening nuclear competition with [[Sanrobonia]] and political turbulence within the dictatorship of [[Potocsí]]. Balisca conducted their first nuclear test on 22 June 1965, but this information was kept secret from the public.  

The nuclear program accelerated significantly as Potocsino aggression increased, particularly following the the [[Camboriú War]] and the [[Bight of Ayorin Crisis]]. Balisca later tested it's first {{W|hydrogen bomb}} in 1978, and it was publicly revealed. The revelation of Balisca's nuclear capabilities during a period of lingering tension raised the prospect of a large scale {{W|Mutually assured destruction|nuclear exchange}}, but this was dismissed by Secretary General [[Mário Sá Justino]], who clarified that Balisca would not use nuclear weapons unless it was attacked with them first ("{{W|No first use}}").

Balisca signed the [[w:Partial Nuclear Test Ban Treaty|Partial Nuclear Test Ban Treaty]] in 1963, and it signed and ratified the [[w:Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty|Comprehensive Nuclear-Test-Ban Treaty]] in 1993 and 1994 respectively. The Baliscan Confederation is an original signatory of the 1972 [[w:Biological Weapons Convention|Biological Weapons Convention]] (BWC). The Baliscan government has denied having or ever developing [[chemical weapons]], and ratified the [[w:Chemical Weapons Convention|Chemical Weapons Convention]] (CWC) in 1993. 

The Baliscan government, specifically under the premiership of [[Zavier Bilal]] has strongly advocated for the expansion of international protocols to prevent the [[w:Militarization of space|militarization of space]], such as the [[w:Moon Treaty|Moon Treaty]] (which Balisca has signed onto, but not yet ratified), and the [[w:Outer Space Treaty|Outer Space Treaty]].

